# What must never enter the build context.
#
# Two jobs: keep secrets and PII out of an image that gets pushed to a
# registry, and keep the context small so builds stay fast. Everything else in
# backend/ IS needed at runtime -- this app is plain ESM with no build step, so
# the source files are the artifact.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
# Service-account keys must never be baked into an image. Cloud Run uses the
# service's own identity; a key file in a layer is a credential that cannot be
# rotated and is readable by anyone who can pull the image.
*service-account*.json
*sa-key*.json
gcp-*.json

# -------------------------------------------------------------- dependencies
# Reinstalled in the image against the lockfile. Copying the host's tree would
# also carry Windows/macOS native builds of bcrypt into a Linux container.
node_modules
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# ------------------------------------------------------- runtime data (PII)
# Employee documents, avatars and rotated logs. Generated at runtime, and in
# the case of uploads and attachments they are real identity documents.
uploads
attachments
logs
*.log

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ git/meta
.git
.gitignore
.dockerignore
Dockerfile
*.md
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
